# Install and Basic Use

## 1. Unpack or Clone the Artifact

Place the artifact on a Linux machine with AMD Vitis HLS 2023.2 installed.

If you plan to reproduce the Table II resource section, ensure that Vivado 2023.2
and a valid ZCU102 license are also installed.

An optional Docker environment is provided under
`artifact/docker/ubuntu22-vitis/` if you prefer to run the artifact inside a
container with host-mounted Xilinx tools.

## 2. Before Starting, Set Up FIFOAdvisor

Before running the artifact workflows, initialize the FIFOAdvisor environment
from the repository root:

```bash
source artifact/fifoadvisor/setup_env.sh
```

This script creates the required environment and installs FIFOAdvisor
automatically. It also installs the LightningSim package declared in
`artifact/fifoadvisor/environment.yml`.

## 3. Check the Environment

From the repository root, run:

```bash
artifact/check_environment.sh
```

The script checks for the expected repository layout and reports whether
`vitis_hls` is available on `PATH`.

## 4. Reproduce Table I

Table I is reproduced with a dedicated HLS/cosim script that uses the
memory-interface kernel variants and generates multi-transaction testbenches for
II measurement:

```bash
artifact/table1/run_table1.py
```

To run one benchmark:

```bash
artifact/table1/run_table1.py --benchmark ResNet8
```

MobileNetV2 and the YOLO benchmarks can take days to complete in HLS/cosim,
depending on the machine and Vitis installation.

## 5. Reproduce Table II

Run the proposed-method FIFO size and timing flow for all benchmarks:

```bash
artifact/table2/run_table2_ste.py
```

To run one benchmark:

```bash
artifact/table2/run_table2_ste.py --benchmark ResNet8
```

Run the FIFOAdvisor comparison flow for all benchmarks:

```bash
artifact/table2/run_table2_fifoadvisor.py
```

To run one benchmark:

```bash
artifact/table2/run_table2_fifoadvisor.py --benchmark ResNet8
```

Run the Table II resource flow for all benchmarks:

```bash
artifact/table2/run_table2_resources.py
```

To run one benchmark:

```bash
artifact/table2/run_table2_resources.py --benchmark ResNet8
```

The Table II resource section additionally requires Vivado 2023.2 and a valid
ZCU102 license.

## 6. Reproduce Table III

Run the Table III flow for all benchmarks:

```bash
artifact/table3/run_table3.py
```

To run one benchmark:

```bash
artifact/table3/run_table3.py --benchmark ResNet8
```

Outputs are written under `artifact/table3/results/`.
